& [VerbatimUserMessage] is the preserved dictation
  + [text] is "can inference juggle multiple different identity objects having the same identity type and keep them individuated cleanly and tracked for when the intention arises to point at them? that is, does the inference engine keep them bound to their intended purposes and resurface the existing identity reliably when called on? that is, does it have a reliable pointer system running behind the inference engine?"

& [VerbatimUserClarification] is the preserved continuation
  + [text] is "my main concern is in handling a basket of things when some are of the same type but have different identity, that there is an accounting for them... that's the right objective"

& [ProvisionalBoundary]
  + [transformer_capacity] is soft contextual entity binding and content-addressed retrieval over token-position representations
  + [nonclaim] is no guaranteed durable object pointer registry native to ordinary autoregressive inference
  + [failure_modes] include alias collision distractor capture state overwrite ambiguous coreference long-context decay and invented re-identification
  + [candidate_architecture] is an external EntityRegistry with stable IDs aliases types roles purposes state provenance constraints and version history
  + [primary_objective] is conservation and accounting of individuated members within a typed collection
  + [execution_boundary] is that the LLM may propose a reference while a resolver binds or rejects it and Judgment validates consequential use
